<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Kamil Muhammad of Mayyafariqin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1260</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> Muhammad was the last Ayyubid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a> in the Jazira, son of al-Muzaffar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a>. He refused to submit to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, who besieged Mayyafariqin from 1258 until it fell in 1260. He was executed and his head was paraded through Syrian cities, ending the principality.</p></div>
